  <prompt>
    Implement FR-08: on Load, a NEW server-side Open XML pre-parse component collects each
    paragraph's `w14:paraId` from the source `.docx`, and mints an OOXML-valid id for every
    paragraph that lacks one. This is the identity substrate the whole E2 track (and the E1
    delta-save splice) depends on: paraId is the stable key that maps editor paragraphs back to
    original OOXML paragraphs. The pre-parse runs alongside the existing mammoth convert inside
    `ComposeService.LoadAsync` (`ComposeService.cs:168`) and produces an ordered `paraId →
    paragraph` map that the Load response carries to the client (task 011 consumes it). Minted ids
    MUST be valid `w14:paraId` values — a random 32-bit `ST_LongHexNumber` with `0 &lt; x &lt;
    0x80000000` — and MUST be collision-checked against every id already present in the part
    (including ids on paragraphs inside table cells and nested tables). The Open XML SDK exposes
    `Paragraph.ParagraphId` but ships **no generator** (Open-XML-SDK #962), so we own the generator.
    Do NOT rely on Word/TipTap to assign ids — this server pre-parse is the load-time id owner (S2).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET 8 developer fluent in the Microsoft Open XML SDK 3.x (`DocumentFormat.OpenXml`) and
    the WordprocessingML `w14:paraId` / `ST_LongHexNumber` markup (MS-DOCX spec), comfortable
    walking a `WordprocessingDocument` body incl. table-cell / nested-table paragraphs, and fluent
    in the Spaarke `Services/Compose/` seams (`ComposeService.LoadAsync`, `SpeFileStore` facade).
  </role>

  <goal>
    A NEW pre-parse component in `Services/Compose/` that, given the load-time `.docx` byte stream,
    returns an ordered `paraId → paragraph-position` map in which EVERY body paragraph (incl.
    table-cell and nested-table paragraphs) has a unique `w14:paraId`: existing ids are collected
    verbatim; missing ids are minted as OOXML-valid random 32-bit values (`0 &lt; x &lt; 0x80000000`)
    that are collision-checked against all ids already in the part. `ComposeService.LoadAsync`
    (`ComposeService.cs:168`) is extended to invoke the pre-parse and project the map onto the Load
    response for the client (task 011) to carry as hidden node attributes. Matching unit tests in
    `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/` assert uniqueness, OOXML-validity of minted
    ids, collision-avoidance, and table-cell coverage; a through-the-wire slice test (NFR-06) proves
    the Load response carries a complete paraId map.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      E2 (`w14:paraId` identity) is the substrate E1's delta save needs — paraId is the splice key
      (design §4.2, §5, §8). S1/S1b proved Docxodus `WmlComparer` **preserves**
      `w14:paraId` on unchanged paragraphs (incl. table cells + nested tables + 3-level numbering),
      so a stable id minted at Load survives the round-trip. S2 proved `@tiptap/extension-unique-id`
      does NOT auto-assign ids to `setContent`-loaded nodes, so **the server pre-parse owns load-time
      ids** (this task) and the client extension owns split/merge minting (task 011). mammoth
      flattens `.docx` to HTML and **discards** `w14:paraId` (`docxBridge.ts`), which is exactly why a
      server-side Open XML pre-parse must run alongside the convert to capture the ids before they are
      lost. `w14:paraId` is `ST_LongHexNumber`, unique within the part, `0 &lt; x &lt; 0x80000000`;
      it is assigned on creation and preserved across edits (its sibling `w14:textId` refreshes on
      content change — not needed here). The Open XML SDK is ALREADY a BFF dependency, so this task
      adds no publish size for the pre-parse itself; task 001 has already added Docxodus + bumped
      OpenXml to 3.5.1 (dep). Still measure + report publish size per §10.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ParaIdPreParser.cs — NEW pre-parse component (this task): Open XML walk collecting/minting w14:paraId, incl. table-cell + nested-table paragraphs; returns the ordered paraId map</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs — LoadAsync (ComposeService.cs:168) invokes the pre-parse alongside the mammoth convert and projects the paraId map onto the Load response</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationReader.cs — existing server-side Open XML body/table walk (reads w:ins/w:del/w:comment regardless of authorship); mirror its part-traversal + table-cell descent pattern, do NOT reimplement a divergent walk</file>
      <file role="canonical-reuse">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationWriter.cs — reference for how Services/Compose operates on byte[] streams behind the facade (no Graph types)</file>
      <file role="reference">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/notes/spikes/ — S1/S1b (paraId preservation on unchanged paragraphs incl. table/nested-table) + S2 (server pre-parse owns load-time ids); the validated substrate this task productionizes</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/design.md §5 (E2 paraId identity), §2 (Current State — anchoring rows: compose-contracts.ts:108-115 + AnnotationReanchorService.cs), §8 (LOAD pipeline), §10 (reuse map)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="pending">Adds `Docxodus` 7.1.0 (SkiaSharp excluded) + bumps `DocumentFormat.OpenXml` 3.4.1 → 3.5.1 and establishes the publish-size + CVE baseline. This task's Open XML pre-parse builds on the 3.5.1 SDK surface; do not add packages here.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-08">Every body paragraph — INCLUDING paragraphs inside table cells and nested tables — MUST have a unique `w14:paraId` after Load. Existing ids are collected verbatim; only missing ids are minted.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-08 / MS-DOCX spec">Minted ids MUST be OOXML-valid `w14:paraId`: a random 32-bit `ST_LongHexNumber` with `0 &lt; x &lt; 0x80000000`, and MUST be collision-checked against every id already present in the part before assignment.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">No `Microsoft.Graph` types above the `SpeFileStore`/Infrastructure facade. The pre-parse operates on `byte[]`/`Stream` only; all SPE access stays behind the existing facade — never a `GraphServiceClient`, `DriveItem`, or other `Microsoft.Graph` type in `Services/Compose/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-05">`Services/Compose/` MUST NOT inject `IOpenAiClient`, executor types, or `IConsumerRoutingService`. This is a deterministic OOXML operation with zero AI reach. Tier-1 NetArchTest enforces.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Keep DI additions minimal — the pre-parser may be a single registered service; internal helpers (id generator, collision set) need not be DI-registered. Register unconditionally (no feature gate) so LoadAsync's dependency is symmetric (CLAUDE.md §10 F.1 asymmetric-registration rule).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029 / NFR-01 / CLAUDE.md §10">Measure BFF publish size on this BFF-touching task: `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`; report absolute compressed size + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (state the PDB convention). ≤60 MB ceiling; ≥+5 MB single-task delta → justify. Verify no new HIGH CVE (`dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06">Ships a through-the-wire `WebApplicationFactory` seam slice test (`tests/integration/seam/**`) proving the Load response carries a complete paraId map for a formatted doc — unit-green ≠ done. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration/ctor-null tests (ADR-038).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-08">The pre-parse adds negligible latency to Load; do not re-parse the document multiple times — a single Open XML pass collects + mints.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / §10 Placement Justification">State the Placement Justification for the new pre-parse component in the PR description, citing `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` decision criteria. Run `/conflict-check` before the BFF PR (LoadAsync is a shared seam; parallel-safe=false).</constraint>
  </constraints>

