  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + dependency check">Confirm task 001 merged (Docxodus + OpenXml 3.5.1 present). Read S1/S1b/S2 spike notes + design §5/§8. Output the FULL rigor-level declaration. Load the knowledge files + `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` before designing.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Design the paraId map contract">Define the ordered `paraId → paragraph-position` map the pre-parse returns and the additive Load-response field that carries it to the client. Keep the DTO in `Services/Compose/`; mirror it to the client contract shape task 011 consumes (do not invent a parallel schema).</step>
    <step order="2" name="Implement ParaIdPreParser">Open the source `.docx` with the Open XML SDK; walk the body incl. table-cell + nested-table paragraphs (mirror `DocxAnnotationReader`'s descent). Collect existing `w14:paraId`s into a seen-set; for each paragraph lacking one, mint a random 32-bit id `0 &lt; x &lt; 0x80000000`, reject-and-retry on collision with the seen-set, then assign + add to the set. Single pass; deterministic; no SkiaSharp / Docxodus `HtmlToWml` path.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Wire into LoadAsync">Extend `ComposeService.LoadAsync` (`ComposeService.cs:168`) to invoke the pre-parse alongside the mammoth convert and project the ordered paraId map onto the Load response. Register the pre-parser unconditionally in the Compose DI module.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Unit tests">Author `ParaIdPreParserTests` in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/`: assert every paragraph (incl. table-cell + nested-table) has a unique id; minted ids are `0 &lt; x &lt; 0x80000000`; existing ids preserved verbatim; a forced-collision fixture proves the retry avoids duplicates. Real docx round-trip; no transport mocks (ADR-038).</step>
    <step order="5" name="Through-the-wire slice test (NFR-06)">Add a `WebApplicationFactory` Load slice test in `tests/integration/seam/**` that GETs the real Load route for a formatted fixture and asserts the response carries a complete paraId map (one id per body paragraph, incl. table cells).</step>
    <step order="6" name="Verify + size/CVE report">Build BFF + run the new tests. Run publish-size + CVE, report absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (state PDB convention). Run the NetArchTest facade check (Services/Compose has no AI-internal injection; no Graph type). Update TASK-INDEX status.</step>
  </steps>

