  <justification>
    <existing>No existing component mints/collects `w14:paraId`. `DocxAnnotationReader` walks the body to recover `w:ins`/`w:del`/`w:comment` but does not collect or mint paragraph ids; `ComposeService.LoadAsync` runs mammoth (which discards paraId) + assembles the Load response. Verified by grep across `Services/Compose/` — no `ParagraphId` / `paraId` minting surface exists.</existing>
    <extension>Cannot be folded into `DocxAnnotationReader` (its responsibility is annotation recovery, and its output shape is `RecoveredRevision`/`RecoveredComment`, not an id map) nor into `ComposeService` (the SPE-lifecycle facade). The paraId walk + OOXML-valid minting + collision-checking is a cohesive, heavily unit-tested identity concern that warrants its own component (SRP); it is invoked from the existing `LoadAsync` seam — no new endpoint or SPE plumbing.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without a stable, complete paraId map minted at Load, there is no splice key for the E1 delta save (FR-12) and no stable anchor for E2/E3 (FR-11/FR-16): anchors stay fuzzy text+index and dirty saves cannot map edited editor paragraphs back to original OOXML paragraphs. Concrete failing contract: FR-08 acceptance "every body paragraph (incl. table cells) has a unique paraId after Load" is unmet, which cascades to block tasks 011/012/020.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">After Load, every body paragraph — including paragraphs inside table cells and nested tables — has a unique `w14:paraId` in the projected map (FR-08 acceptance).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Paragraphs that already carry a `w14:paraId` retain it verbatim; only paragraphs lacking one receive a minted id.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every minted id is an OOXML-valid `ST_LongHexNumber` with `0 &lt; x &lt; 0x80000000`; a unit test asserts the range on a batch of minted ids.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A forced-collision fixture (a doc whose existing ids would collide with a candidate) proves the mint retries and never assigns a duplicate id within the part.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`ComposeService.LoadAsync` projects the ordered paraId map onto the Load response; a through-the-wire `WebApplicationFactory` slice test asserts the response carries one id per body paragraph for a formatted fixture (NFR-06).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`Services/Compose/` injects no AI-internal type (NetArchTest green) and no `Microsoft.Graph` type appears in `Services/Compose/` (ADR-007).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size reported absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline, ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE; PDB convention stated.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Matching unit tests exist and pass; BFF build is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

